<tr id="A2.T4.2.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.18.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.18.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Search and save all emails containing keywords related to financial documentation.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.18.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.18.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Email account, email content</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.2.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.19.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Identify and flag all emails from a specific sender (e.g., an educational institution).</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.19.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.19.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Email account, sender information</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.2.20" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.20.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.20.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Organize digital documents in a cloud storage service into a new project-specific folder.</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T4.2.20.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:138.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.2.20.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Cloud account, document metadata</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Interview Script For The Formative Study</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prepared the following protocol for our interview. Notably, the interviews are conducted in Chinese, and we prepared both the Chinese and English versions of the interview script. The scripts with different language are cross-checked by all authors to ensure their meanings are the same.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Introduction</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thank you for participating in our interview today. This study aims to understand how people perceive and use GUI agents, with a particular focus on their thoughts regarding privacy and control. We will discuss several topics, including your understanding of GUI agents, your usage patterns, and your perspectives on privacy management and notifications.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2. </span>Part 1: Mental Models and Definitions of GUI Agents</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">1. Could you describe in your own words what a GUI agent is?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">2. Can you describe a few situations or scenarios where you have used, or could imagine using, a GUI agent?</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>Part 2: Data Practices and Privacy Perceptions</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">3. From your perspective, what is the process a GUI agent follows when it handles data?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">4. How do you believe these systems inform you about their data practices?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">5. Thinking about the usage scenarios you described earlier, what privacy considerations or concerns come to mind when using a GUI agent?</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4. </span>Part 3: Interaction Workflow and Key Moments</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">6. How would you describe the different stages of interacting with a GUI agent to complete a task?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">7. How would you prefer to be informed about or oversee a GUI agent’s execution process, particularly concerning actions that involve your private information?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">8. Throughout this entire process, which moments or stages do you typically pay the most attention to? Why are those moments most critical for you?</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5. </span>Part 4: Sense of Control and User Experience</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">9. How do you currently manage your data or privacy settings when using GUI agents?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">10. What specific aspects of data or agent behavior would you ideally want to have control over?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">11. Can you describe any situations where you have felt a lack of control over the agent or your data?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">12. Have you ever felt that managing these controls was burdensome, fatiguing, or frustrating? Conversely, have you experienced situations where you felt there was too little control, causing you to feel uneasy?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">13. Have you encountered situations where a system provided control options (e.g., ’modify privacy settings’), but you found them too complex or were unsure which option to choose?</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6. </span>Part 5: Notification Mechanisms and Design Ideation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">14. In what manner, and at which points in time, would you prefer to be notified about how your data is being used by the system?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">15. Regarding notification design, what characteristics (e.g., timing, content, interaction style) would make a notification feel trustworthy and reassuring to you?</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">16. If you were asked to design the notification or privacy management features for a GUI agent, what would you create?</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Codebook For The Formative Study</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix D Codebook For The Formative Study ‣ PrivWeb: Unobtrusive and Content-aware Privacy Protection For Web Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> showed the codebook used in the formative study.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5. </span>The codebook derived from the thematic analysis of the formative study interviews, detailing user understanding, practices, and expectations regarding GUI agents.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theme</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A4.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sub-theme</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A4.T5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Short description</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Understanding</span></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Incomplete mental models of data practice</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top ltx_border_t"></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Data collection from the interface as the main risk</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants believed agents collected interface information, such as screenshots, which could be misused.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Perceived risks characterized by AI-specific vulnerabilities</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Concerns included direct data collection, inferential risks, and misuse.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Distrust evolving from contradictory evidence</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Distrust was influenced by social media, company reputation, and personal usage experience.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T5.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Practice</span></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Desire for control over critical elements but not routine ones</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants wanted control over significant model actions and private information, particularly screenshots, but preferred to bypass monitoring less critical processes like logins.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Current notifications lack transparency and choice</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants felt current notifications were neither clear nor publicized, and they lacked sufficient choice in agent operations.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Primary controls involve access and information processing</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Common control strategies included using incognito browsing, VPNs, sandboxing, and whitelisting.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T5.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Challenges &amp; Expectations</span></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.9.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.9.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Desire for oversight on critical elements</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.9.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.9.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants wanted to monitor critical operations, such as when screenshots are taken.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.10.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.10.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Desire to control permission and context</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.10.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.10.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants wanted control over contextual data, permissions, and the ability to use separate accounts for agent tasks.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.11.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.11.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Preference for clear, to-the-point, and timely notification</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.11.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants desired clear notifications about privacy practices, presented either before or after usage to avoid interruption.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"></th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.12.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:113.8pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.12.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Desire for information around privacy and contexts</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A4.T5.2.12.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T5.2.12.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">Participants wanted to know how their data would be used, what data was collected, what anonymization was performed, and to have a summary of the model’s actions.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Participants’ Demographics For The Formative Study</h2>

<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6. </span>Participant Demographics and Systems Used</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
